<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Josip Jelačić</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1801–1859</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Josip Jelačić was ban of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> from 1848 to 1859 and a general in the Austrian army. In the revolutions of 1848 he led Croatian forces against the Hungarian revolutionary government and helped crush the uprising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfdom">Serfdom</a> in Croatia was abolished early in his time as ban. His equestrian statue stands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagreb">Zagreb</a>'s main square, which bears his name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/josip-jelacic.jpg" alt="Josip Jelačić" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ivan Zasche (1826-1863) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ban-josip-jelacic.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
